    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Reads Settings + Posts, checks pause, plans today's post slots.\nconst s = $('Get Settings1').first().json;\nconst posts = $('Get Posts').all().map(i => i.json).filter(p => p.id);\nconst isTrue = v => String(v).trim().toUpperCase() === 'TRUE';\nif (isTrue(s.paused)) return [];                       // pause button\n\nconst tz = s.timezone || 'Asia/Kolkata';\nconst [ws, we] = String(s.work_hours || '9-18').split(/[^0-9]+/).filter(Boolean).map(Number);\nconst perDay = Number(s.posts_per_day) || 1;\nconst gapH = Math.max(Number(s.post_gap_hours) || 4, 4); // PDF: at least 4 h\n\n// Plan for today; if today's working hours are over (or weekend), plan for next weekday\nconst now = DateTime.now().setZone(tz);\nlet day = now;\nif (now.weekday > 5 || now.hour >= we - 1) {\n  day = now.plus({ days: 1 });\n  while (day.weekday > 5) day = day.plus({ days: 1 });\n}\nconst dayStr = day.toISODate();\nconst dayEnd = day.set({ hour: we, minute: 0, second: 0, millisecond: 0 });\n\nconst sameDay = posts.filter(p =>\n  ['pending', 'approved', 'published'].includes(String(p.status)) && p.scheduled_at &&\n  DateTime.fromISO(String(p.scheduled_at), { zone: tz }).toISODate() === dayStr);\nconst need = perDay - sameDay.length;\nif (need <= 0) return [];                              // daily post limit reached\n\nconst last = sameDay.map(p => DateTime.fromISO(String(p.scheduled_at), { zone: tz })).sort((a, b) => b - a)[0];\nlet slot = last ? last.plus({ hours: gapH })\n                : day.set({ hour: ws + 1, minute: 0, second: 0, millisecond: 0 });\n\nconst recent = posts.slice(-10).map(p => String(p.text || '').split('\\n')[0]).filter(Boolean);\n\nconst prompt = `You write LinkedIn posts for the company page of YOUR_COMPANY_NAME, which sells a learning management system (LMS).\nBrand voice: helpful, practical, plain English, no hype.\nTarget audience: ${s.target_audience}\n\nWrite ONE LinkedIn post that is useful to this audience on its own, even if they never buy anything.\n\nStructure:\n1. hook: max 200 characters, includes the primary keyword, makes them want to read on.\n2. content: 4-8 short paragraphs. A real problem this audience has, why it matters, 3-5 practical tips. Mention an LMS at most once, softly, as one option.\n3. cta: one question inviting comments. No links, no \"DM me\".\n4. hashtags: 3-5 (mix broad and niche), without spaces.\n\nSEO: pick 1 primary keyword and 2-3 secondary keywords and use them naturally.\nRules: no false claims, no invented statistics or numbers, no hype words, no links, 150-250 words total, max 2 emojis.\nPlain text only: no markdown, never use ** or * for bold or italics (LinkedIn shows them as symbols). For lists use \"1.\" or \"→\".\nDo NOT repeat these recent hooks/topics: ${recent.join(' | ') || 'none'}\n\nCheck your post against every rule before answering.\n5. image_prompt: a detailed prompt for ONE realistic, professional photo that fits this post (education / workplace setting, natural light, vertical 4:5, no text, no logos, no brand names).\n\nAnswer ONLY with JSON: {\"topic\":\"\",\"primary_keyword\":\"\",\"hook\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"cta\":\"\",\"hashtags\":[],\"image_prompt\":\"\"}`;\n\nconst out = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < need && slot < dayEnd; i++) {\n  out.push({ json: { id: 'P' + Date.now() + i, scheduled_at: slot.toISO(), prompt } });\n  slot = slot.plus({ hours: gapH });\n}\nreturn out;\n"
      },
